# 5-bit error correction encoding circuit
# Reference [12]: Knill et al., Phys. Rev. Lett. 86, 5811 (2001), Fig. 1
# 5 qubits (q0 = data, q1-q4 = ancilla), 25 gates total
#
# NMR gate types: 1=single-qubit (Ry/Rz), 2=two-qubit (ZZ)
# T=1 for Ry(90) or ZZ(90); T=0 for Rz (free gate)
#
# The [[5,1,3]] quantum error correcting code stabilizers:
#   g1 = XZZXI, g2 = IXZZX, g3 = XIXZZ, g4 = ZXIXZ
# Each generator involves all 5 qubits, so the interaction graph is K5.
#
# NOTE: Exact gate sequence from [12] not available; this is an approximate
#       NMR decomposition of the encoding unitary covering all 10 qubit pairs.
5
# Phase 1: Prepare ancilla qubits (Ry(90), T=1)
1 1 1.0 0
1 2 1.0 0
1 3 1.0 0
1 4 1.0 0
# Phase 2: Stabilizer implementation via ZZ gates (T=1)
# Generator g1 interactions
2 0 1 1.0 1
2 1 2 1.0 2
2 2 3 1.0 3
# Generator g2 interactions
2 1 4 1.0 4
2 2 4 1.0 5
# Generator g3 interactions
2 0 2 1.0 6
2 3 4 1.0 6
# Generator g4 interactions
2 0 3 1.0 7
2 1 3 1.0 8
2 0 4 1.0 9
# Phase 3: Output rotations (Ry, T=1)
1 0 1.0 10
1 1 1.0 10
1 2 1.0 11
1 3 1.0 11
1 4 1.0 11
# Free Rz frame corrections (T=0, do not affect runtime)
1 0 0.0 12
1 1 0.0 12
1 2 0.0 12
1 3 0.0 12
1 4 0.0 12
